From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:00:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: show HDR content as EDR on the J604
 panel (opt-in)

The J604 panel reaches 1600 cd/m2 for HDR content (ADT /backlight
LmaxProduct) above a 600 nit SDR maximum, and macOS shows HDR on it as
EDR: SDR white stays at the level the user chose while the panel level
rises, and each swap carries the display EDR scale and the headroom the
frame uses. Aurora drives the same words on the desktop 26.x panels
(ae07fd5bb6 "Show HDR content as EDR on desktop 26.x panels", 7e6b33aa91,
43f112d09a: dcp_edr_prepare()); the 26.6.2 A407 record of the T8132
backend opens with that dcp_swap layout, so the words sit at the same
offsets: the panel level at +0x35e (bl_update +0x354), the brightness
limit at +0x376 (bl_flags[1]), the EDR scale at +0x37e (bl_flags[2]) and
the headroom used at +0x3e6 (bl_flags[4]).

Port it to iomfb_m4, behind appledrm.panel_edr (default off):

- dcp-m4-edr.h: the words and the per-swap state of dcp_edr_prepare(),
  on the helpers of dcp-edr.h: H rises one step per swap up to
  peak / SDR white, never above the ADT potential headroom (16.0 on the
  J604), a brightness change carries SDR white x H, EDR ends in one swap,
  and the ramp starts again from 1.0 after a blank.
- With the parameter, a P3 panel whose ADT peak lies above the SDR
  maximum gets a third EDID block (CTA-861: BT.2020 RGB, HDR static
  metadata for SDR and PQ, the peak as maximum luminance) and the
  Colorspace and HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA properties. The atomic check takes
  SDR, and PQ only on such a panel; the panel shows EDR while PQ and
  BT.2020 RGB are both set (Aurora 10c70d091f: Hyprland leaves the PQ
  metadata when it goes back to SDR).
- An EDR frame's surface is tagged BT.2020 / PQ (primaries 9, transfer
  16, as the desktop backend tags it) instead of P3-D65 / sRGB (12, 13),
  and idle caching is skipped while EDR runs.

The peak comes from the ADT, not from the firmware (A128 on the desktop
backend), which this backend does not ask yet. Without the parameter the
connector, the EDID, the atomic check and every swap byte stay as they
were: no SDR frame carries the words, and the colour tags keep their
values. debugfs iomfb_m4 shows the EDR state when the parameter is set.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
(cherry picked from commit f00440d9c128cc63193b3497205cd098a1ec3013)
[j604: k610 drm sync: apple_drv.c conflict with Aurora's
 apple_connector_attach_hdr() (external DP/HDMI HDR, desktop 26.x panel
 EDR, PQ_REFERENCE_LUMINANCE on eDP): the separate attach_edr() is
 dropped and the T8132 panel with appledrm.panel_edr is passed to
 apple_connector_attach_hdr() as a panel that shows PQ as EDR, so it also
 gets PQ_REFERENCE_LUMINANCE = 100 (the same SDR-white-at-PQ-100 model).
 Upstream's dcp_crtc_check_hdr() now runs before the T8132 branch of
 dcp_crtc_atomic_check() and refuses PQ on a modeset unless the panel is
 a desktop EDR panel or an external sink with a PQ mode; it now also
 takes PQ when iomfb_m4_panel_edr_capable() (new: internal T8132 panel,
 EDR capable). iomfb_m4_atomic_check_hdr() leaves an external T8132 DCP
 to upstream's check. Default unchanged: panel_edr=0, so no Colorspace /
 HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA on the J604 eDP connector and no EDR words.]

(cherry picked from commit b443a50936b69ebb4db2cd4b1fab9738aba43bb8)
(cherry picked from commit b6bdf6545d07643c497c35e7a1b444ea33163ef2)
